<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila affinis Turing wavenumber at 2.4 µm (Holocene, detail tier) — MorphoEval overall 86.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 bisects Du at Dv/Du = 10 until the fastest linear mode is 2.443 µm. The periodic Schnakenberg field then selects 2.432 µm by Fourier peak (reference 2.444 µm). The determinant-minimizing wavelength at the same diffusivities is 2.251 µm and is not substituted for the pattern wavelength. Continuum versus discrete sigma(k): Pearson r = 0.9991, RMSE = 0.0117. Ablation Dv = Du gives sigma_max = -0.099. Ratio sweep at fixed classical wavelength is monotonic in peak growth rate. Specimen foreground fraction 0.221 versus last-frame 0.299; orientation KS = 0.0025 against a 0.05 reference. Image-fitness CV similarity of the 12-frame 960 px GIF against the CC BY-SA habitus is 96.0. Weighted overall 86.2. Overall 86.2/100 (faithfulness 85.3, reproducibility 88.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 87, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/gif, 2087759 B, 960×720 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 7605e3d489c1c2272c692089bfcc27941a33b01aa6f91110971df3b15553afa7 (sha256 7605e3d489c1c2272c692089bfcc27941a33b01aa6f91110971df3b15553afa7), spec_fingerprint 1d549b7322f4ffdb1233c8d9a23519c69dfd24ec8235a0131e1cb9b06ccb909d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 1d549b7322f4ffdb1233c8d9a23519c69dfd24ec8235a0131e1cb9b06ccb909d; artifact_sha256: 7605e3d489c1c2272c692089bfcc27941a33b01aa6f91110971df3b15553afa7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_affinis_specimen.jpg=83062d706a605b86..., datasets/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=9939928504f37754..., datasets/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=368c8326ecee5c1b..., datasets/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=2164e988b14e5446...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: the critical wavenumber and the requirement that the inhibitor diffuse faster than the activator. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics and the Gierer-Meinhardt activator-inhibitor reading. | Murray 1981: the selected length is a diffusion scale. Kondo and Miura 2010 review the same framework. | Sturtevant 1916 and Miller 1955 establish the species and its sex-comb diagnosis.; reconstructed_in_script: Du = 0.05101 µm^2/time, Dv = 0.5101 µm^2/time, chosen so argmax sigma(k) is 2.443 µm. | Nonlinear FFT wavelength 2.432 µm on a 160 by 120 periodic grid, seed 3174, 4500 steps. | Length ratios 2.444/98.43 = 0.0248 versus berryi and 2.444/138.7 = 0.0176 versus americana.; transfer_boundary: Pigment-granule ontogeny is taken from Shoup 1966 on D. melanogaster and is not re-measured here. | Tergite pigment genetics (Wittkopp 2002, 2003) operate at a coarser scale than 2.444 µm. | The adult frame of the GIF is the photograph. Computer-vision similarity therefore scores the habitus, not an independently drawn fly.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the determinant-minimizing wavelength (2.251 µm) equals the pattern wavelength (2.432 µm). Both are reported. | Does not claim the sex-comb tooth spacing equals 2.444 µm. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication. No local nanopub profile was present. | Does not claim berryi is the ancestor of affinis or that affinis is the ancestor of americana.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R4 remains open: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent, so nanopubs were built and conformance-checked but not signed.",
        "remediation needed: R5 remains open: one habitus, and the 250 µm scale bar does not resolve 2.444 µm. A second assessor did not score this loop." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.62e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

