<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila affinis Turing wavenumber at 2.4 µm (Holocene, detail tier) (Drosophila affinis)",
        "Drosophila affinis Turing wavenumber at 2.4 µm (Holocene, detail tier) faithfully reproduces Drosophila affinis morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila affinis specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila affinis" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a signed nanopublication. No local nanopub profile was present.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim berryi is the ancestor of affinis or that affinis is the ancestor of americana.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the determinant-minimizing wavelength (2.251 µm) equals the pattern wavelength (2.432 µm). Both are reported.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the sex-comb tooth spacing equals 2.444 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Du = 0.05101 µm^2/time, Dv = 0.5101 µm^2/time, chosen so argmax sigma(k) is 2.443 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Length ratios 2.444/98.43 = 0.0248 versus berryi and 2.444/138.7 = 0.0176 versus americana.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Nonlinear FFT wavelength 2.432 µm on a 160 by 120 periodic grid, seed 3174, 4500 steps.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981: the selected length is a diffusion scale. Kondo and Miura 2010 review the same framework.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics and the Gierer-Meinhardt activator-inhibitor reading.",
        "reported_in_source: Sturtevant 1916 and Miller 1955 establish the species and its sex-comb diagnosis.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: the critical wavenumber and the requirement that the inhibitor diffuse faster than the activator.",
        "transfer_boundary: Pigment-granule ontogeny is taken from Shoup 1966 on D. melanogaster and is not re-measured here.",
        "transfer_boundary: Tergite pigment genetics (Wittkopp 2002, 2003) operate at a coarser scale than 2.444 µm.",
        "transfer_boundary: The adult frame of the GIF is the photograph. Computer-vision similarity therefore scores the habitus, not an independently drawn fly." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila affinis (Nearctic Woodland Obscura Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_affinis_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; organism: Drosophila affinis; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: the critical wavenumber and the requirement that the inhibitor diffuse faster than the activator. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics and the Gierer-Meinhardt activator-inhibitor reading. | Murray 1981: the selected length is a diffusion scale. Kondo and Miura 2010 review the same framework. | Sturtevant 1916 and Miller 1955 establish the species and its sex-comb diagnosis.; reconstructed_in_script: Du = 0.05101 µm^2/time, Dv = 0.5101 µm^2/time, chosen so argmax sigma(k) is 2.443 µm. | Nonlinear FFT wavelength 2.432 µm on a 160 by 120 periodic grid, seed 3174, 4500 steps. | Length ratios 2.444/98.43 = 0.0248 versus berryi and 2.444/138.7 = 0.0176 versus americana.; transfer_boundary: Pigment-granule ontogeny is taken from Shoup 1966 on D. melanogaster and is not re-measured here. | Tergite pigment genetics (Wittkopp 2002, 2003) operate at a coarser scale than 2.444 µm. | The adult frame of the GIF is the photograph. Computer-vision similarity therefore scores the habitus, not an independently drawn fly.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the determinant-minimizing wavelength (2.251 µm) equals the pattern wavelength (2.432 µm). Both are reported. | Does not claim the sex-comb tooth spacing equals 2.444 µm. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication. No local nanopub profile was present. | Does not claim berryi is the ancestor of affinis or that affinis is the ancestor of americana.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
